1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,859
A recipe for two, made for four.

2
00:00:02,859 --> 00:00:05,003
A photo zoomed to double size.

3
00:00:05,003 --> 00:00:07,940
A car going twice as fast, the same way.

4
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:12,624
Each time, one number scales something
up, but its shape or direction stays

5
00:00:12,624 --> 00:00:13,524
the same.

6
00:00:13,809 --> 00:00:16,778
Aarav cruises north at
six metres per second.

7
00:00:16,778 --> 00:00:19,697
His little cousin rides
beside him at three.

8
00:00:20,047 --> 00:00:22,372
Same direction, double the speed.

9
00:00:22,372 --> 00:00:25,335
So is Aarav's velocity
two times his cousin's?

10
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:27,832
And what would minus two times mean?

11
00:00:28,332 --> 00:00:31,612
By the end, you will know what
a plain number does to an arrow.

12
00:00:32,262 --> 00:00:34,532
So what does a scalar do to a vector?

13
00:00:34,882 --> 00:00:38,835
A scalar is a plain number,
like two, or half, or minus one.

14
00:00:39,235 --> 00:00:43,266
Multiply vector A by a number lambda,
and you get a new vector, lambda

15
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:44,166
A.

16
00:00:44,026 --> 00:00:46,972
Its size becomes lambda
times the size of A.

17
00:00:47,372 --> 00:00:50,785
If lambda is positive, it
points the same way as A.

18
00:00:50,785 --> 00:00:54,036
If lambda is negative, it
points the opposite way.

19
00:00:54,686 --> 00:00:56,890
Let's see it on our motion notebook.

20
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,739
Here is vector A, three units
long, pointing north east.

21
00:01:01,139 --> 00:01:02,568
Turn the dial to two.

22
00:01:02,568 --> 00:01:05,916
The arrow stretches to six
units, in the same direction.

23
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,642
Turn it to one half.

24
00:01:07,642 --> 00:01:09,763
It shrinks to one and a half units.

25
00:01:09,763 --> 00:01:11,251
Still the same direction.

26
00:01:11,651 --> 00:01:13,577
Now slide lambda below zero.

27
00:01:13,577 --> 00:01:14,634
Watch closely.

28
00:01:14,634 --> 00:01:18,043
At zero, it shrinks to a
point: the zero vector.

29
00:01:18,543 --> 00:01:20,394
Past zero, it flips around.

30
00:01:20,394 --> 00:01:24,301
At minus one, it is the same
length, but pointing south west.

31
00:01:24,801 --> 00:01:26,450
The graph is a V shape.

32
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:30,170
The size depends only on the
size of lambda, not its sign.

33
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:33,282
Let's write the rules one step at a time.

34
00:01:33,632 --> 00:01:34,532
Step one.

35
00:01:34,448 --> 00:01:35,348
The size.

36
00:01:35,263 --> 00:01:39,767
The magnitude of lambda A equals the
size of lambda, times the magnitude

37
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:40,667
of A.

38
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:42,034
Step two.

39
00:01:42,017 --> 00:01:43,171
The direction.

40
00:01:43,171 --> 00:01:45,218
Lambda above zero keeps it.

41
00:01:45,218 --> 00:01:47,428
Lambda below zero reverses it.

42
00:01:48,178 --> 00:01:49,211
Step three.

43
00:01:49,211 --> 00:01:52,097
Lambda equals minus one gives minus A.

44
00:01:52,847 --> 00:01:53,816
Step four.

45
00:01:53,816 --> 00:01:56,832
In components, every part is multiplied.

46
00:01:56,832 --> 00:02:00,762
Two times two i plus three
j is four i plus six j.

47
00:02:01,512 --> 00:02:02,559
Remember this.

48
00:02:02,559 --> 00:02:05,671
A positive number stretches
or shrinks the arrow.

49
00:02:05,671 --> 00:02:07,834
A negative number also flips it.

50
00:02:08,534 --> 00:02:11,375
Now, why does this matter
so much in physics?

51
00:02:11,725 --> 00:02:14,914
Because many laws are just
a scalar times a vector.

52
00:02:15,314 --> 00:02:18,093
Displacement equals time times velocity.

53
00:02:18,093 --> 00:02:21,503
So displacement points
the same way as velocity.

54
00:02:21,903 --> 00:02:24,528
Force equals mass times acceleration.

55
00:02:24,528 --> 00:02:29,527
Mass is positive, so force and
acceleration always point the same way.

56
00:02:29,927 --> 00:02:32,595
And momentum equals mass times velocity.

57
00:02:32,595 --> 00:02:36,430
The scalar sets the size, the
vector sets the direction.

58
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:40,687
Here is the reasoning link by
link, for Aarav and his cousin.

59
00:02:41,037 --> 00:02:44,601
His cousin's velocity is three
metres per second, north.

60
00:02:45,001 --> 00:02:49,558
Aarav goes in the same direction, so
the number in front must be positive.

61
00:02:49,958 --> 00:02:52,545
His speed is six, two times three.

62
00:02:52,545 --> 00:02:55,615
So Aarav's velocity is
two times his cousin's.

63
00:02:56,215 --> 00:02:57,287
Side by side.

64
00:02:57,287 --> 00:03:01,395
Two times A is twice as long,
and points the same way as A.

65
00:03:01,795 --> 00:03:06,373
Minus two times A is also twice as
long, but points the opposite way.

66
00:03:06,973 --> 00:03:08,014
Now you try.

67
00:03:08,014 --> 00:03:11,411
Do two A and minus two A
have the same magnitude?

68
00:03:11,411 --> 00:03:13,332
Pause the video and decide.

69
00:03:16,532 --> 00:03:17,432
Yes!

70
00:03:17,064 --> 00:03:19,220
Both are twice as long as A.

71
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:23,231
The minus sign changes only
the direction, never the size.

72
00:03:23,881 --> 00:03:25,046
One more idea.

73
00:03:25,046 --> 00:03:27,491
A scalar can even change the unit.

74
00:03:27,841 --> 00:03:32,695
Velocity in metres per second, times a
time in seconds, gives a displacement

75
00:03:32,695 --> 00:03:33,595
in metres.

76
00:03:33,969 --> 00:03:38,098
Aarav cruises at six metres per
second north for four seconds.

77
00:03:38,498 --> 00:03:43,041
Four seconds times six metres per
second is twenty four metres, north.

78
00:03:43,041 --> 00:03:45,686
Same direction, but now a displacement.

79
00:03:46,286 --> 00:03:47,259
Your turn.

80
00:03:47,259 --> 00:03:50,079
Multiply a vector by zero point five.

81
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:52,082
Does its direction change?

82
00:03:52,082 --> 00:03:53,515
Pause and decide.

83
00:03:56,715 --> 00:03:57,615
No.

84
00:03:57,204 --> 00:04:01,145
Zero point five is positive,
so the arrow only shrinks.

85
00:04:01,145 --> 00:04:03,498
Only a negative number flips it.

86
00:04:04,148 --> 00:04:05,884
Now, one worked example.

87
00:04:06,234 --> 00:04:08,671
Vector A is three i plus four j.

88
00:04:08,671 --> 00:04:11,359
Find minus two A, and its magnitude.

89
00:04:11,859 --> 00:04:14,332
Multiply each part by minus two.

90
00:04:15,082 --> 00:04:18,195
Minus two times three i is minus six i.

91
00:04:18,195 --> 00:04:21,365
Minus two times four j is minus eight j.

92
00:04:22,115 --> 00:04:25,442
So minus two A is minus
six i minus eight j.

93
00:04:26,192 --> 00:04:29,950
Its magnitude is the root of
thirty six plus sixty four.

94
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:32,817
Root one hundred is ten: two times five.

95
00:04:33,466 --> 00:04:34,932
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:35,282 --> 00:04:39,983
Many students think that multiplying by
a negative number makes the magnitude

97
00:04:39,983 --> 00:04:40,883
negative.

98
00:04:41,106 --> 00:04:44,082
But a magnitude is a
length, never negative.

99
00:04:44,082 --> 00:04:47,794
The size of minus three A is
three times the size of A.

100
00:04:47,794 --> 00:04:49,503
Only the direction flips.

101
00:04:50,153 --> 00:04:51,645
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:51,645 --> 00:04:56,171
Inside bigger problems: a vector
parallel or opposite to a given one.

103
00:04:56,771 --> 00:04:58,072
Exam level now.

104
00:04:58,072 --> 00:05:00,598
A is two i minus j plus two k.

105
00:05:00,598 --> 00:05:04,624
Which vector has magnitude
six and points opposite to A?

106
00:05:04,624 --> 00:05:05,981
Pause and solve.

107
00:05:11,381 --> 00:05:12,647
The answer is C.

108
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:17,531
The size of A is the root of four
plus one plus four, which is three.

109
00:05:18,031 --> 00:05:20,840
We need size six, so the factor is two.

110
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:22,976
Opposite, so it is minus two.

111
00:05:22,976 --> 00:05:24,865
Minus two A is the answer.

112
00:05:25,465 --> 00:05:26,926
Here is your recap.

113
00:05:26,926 --> 00:05:28,427
Screenshot this card.

114
00:05:31,627 --> 00:05:33,558
Can you answer these without help?

115
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:34,858
One.

116
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:38,373
What happens to a vector when
you multiply it by minus one?

117
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:40,173
Two.

118
00:05:39,834 --> 00:05:43,738
Is the magnitude of minus
five A positive or negative?

119
00:05:44,638 --> 00:05:45,538
Three.

120
00:05:45,286 --> 00:05:49,161
Why do force and acceleration
always point the same way?

121
00:05:50,261 --> 00:05:54,593
Next time: how can one slanted
arrow be split into two parts?

122
00:05:54,593 --> 00:05:57,170
Resolution of vectors into components.
